dhp78:1 starts: Don’t associate with bad friends.
dhp78:2 starts: Don’t associate with the low.
dhp78:3 starts: Associate with admirable friends.
dhp78:4 starts: Associate with the best.
dhp55:1 starts: Sandalwood, tagara,
dhp55:2 starts: lotus, & jasmine:
dhp55:3 starts: among these scents,
dhp55:4 starts: the scent of virtue
dhp60:1 starts: Long for the wakeful is the night.
dhp60:2 starts: Long for the weary, a league.
dhp60:3 starts: For fools
dhp60:4 starts: samsara
dhp64:1 starts: Even if for a lifetime
dhp64:2 starts: the fool stays with the wise,
dhp64:3 starts: he knows nothing of the Dhamma–
dhp64:4 starts: as the ladle,
dhp65:1 starts: Even if for a moment,
dhp65:2 starts: the perceptive person stays with the wise,
dhp65:3 starts: he immediately knows the Dhamma–
dhp65:4 starts: as the tongue,
dhp67:1 starts: It’s not good,
dhp67:2 starts: that, once it’s done,
dhp67:3 starts: whose result you reap crying,
dhp67:4 starts: your face in tears.
dhp68:1 starts: It’s good,
dhp68:2 starts: that, once it’s done,
dhp68:3 starts: whose result you reap gratified,
dhp68:4 starts: happy at heart.
dhp69:1 starts: As long as evil has yet to
dhp69:2 starts: the fool mistakes it for honey.
dhp69:3 starts: But when that evil ripens,
dhp69:4 starts: the fool falls into
dhp74:1 starts: ‘Let householders & those gone forth
dhp74:2 starts: was done by me alone.
dhp74:3 starts: May I alone determine
dhp74:4 starts: what’s a duty, what’s not’:
dhp74:5 starts: the resolve of a fool
dhp74:6 starts: as they grow–
dhp75:1 starts: The path to material gain
dhp75:2 starts: another.
dhp75:3 starts: Realizing this, the monk,
dhp75:4 starts: a disciple to the Awakened One,
dhp75:5 starts: shouldn’t relish offerings,
dhp75:6 starts: should cultivate seclusion
dhp76:1 starts: Regard him as one who
dhp76:2 starts: points out
dhp76:3 starts: the wise one who
dhp76:4 starts: Stay with this sort of sage.
dhp76:5 starts: For the one who stays
dhp76:6 starts: things get better,
dhp79:1 starts: Drinking the Dhamma,
dhp79:2 starts: with clear awareness & calm.
dhp79:3 starts: In the Dhamma revealed
dhp79:4 starts: the wise person
dhp81:1 starts: As a single slab of rock
dhp81:2 starts: won’t budge in the wind,
dhp81:3 starts: so the wise are not moved
dhp81:4 starts: by praise,
dhp86:1 starts: But those who practice Dhamma
dhp86:2 starts: in line with the well-taught Dhamma,
dhp86:3 starts: will cross over
dhp86:4 starts: the realm of Death
dhp88:1 starts: There he should wish for delight,
dhp88:2 starts: discarding sensuality–
dhp88:3 starts: He should cleanse himself–wise–
dhp88:4 starts: of what defiles the mind.
dhp89:1 starts: Whose minds are well-developed
dhp89:2 starts: in the factors for self-awakening,
dhp89:3 starts: who delight in non-clinging,
dhp89:4 starts: relinquishing grasping–
dhp89:5 starts: resplendent,
dhp89:6 starts: they, in the world,
dhp91:1 starts: The mindful keep active,
dhp91:2 starts: don’t delight in settling back.
dhp91:3 starts: They renounce every home,
dhp91:4 starts: like swans taking off from a lake.
dhp92:1 starts: Not hoarding,
dhp92:2 starts: having comprehended food,
dhp92:3 starts: their pasture–emptiness
dhp92:4 starts: & freedom without sign:
dhp92:5 starts: their course,
dhp92:6 starts: like that of birds through space,
dhp93:1 starts: Effluents ended,
dhp93:2 starts: independent of nutriment,
dhp93:3 starts: their pasture–emptiness
dhp93:4 starts: & freedom without sign:
dhp93:5 starts: their trail,
dhp93:6 starts: like that of birds through space,
dhp96:1 starts: Calm is his mind,
dhp96:2 starts: calm his speech
dhp96:3 starts: one who’s released through right knowing,
dhp96:4 starts: pacified,
dhp98:1 starts: In village or wilds,
dhp98:2 starts: valley, plateau:
dhp98:3 starts: that place is delightful
dhp98:4 starts: where arahants dwell.
dhp103:1 starts: Greater in battle
dhp103:2 starts: than the man who would conquer
dhp103:3 starts: is he who would conquer
dhp103:4 starts: himself.
